---
Run the examples of checked decisions through the whole engine.

The bundled catalog and the project's `.lighthouse/decisions`. Examples run in each language whose plugin the config lists (or only in --language); a decision needs an example for every language run. Exits 1 when any example fails.

Usage: lighthouse decision test [OPTIONS] [IDS]...

Arguments:
  [IDS]...
          Decisions to test: ids and globs. Default: every checked decision

Options:
      --config <FILE>
          The project file; the project root is then the current directory
          
          [env: LIGHTHOUSE_CONFIG=]

      --language <LANGUAGE>
          Run the examples in this language only

      --color <COLOR>
          Color of help and messages. `auto` honours NO_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE
          
          [env: LIGHTHOUSE_COLOR=]
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --format <FORMAT>
          `text` for people, `json` for programs (its schema: `lighthouse schema`)

          Possible values:
          - text: The human form
          - json: One JSON document on one line
          
          [default: text]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
